When asked about the name change, the Harlem rapper attributed the decision to &#8220;growth&#8221; and suggested that A$AP Mob was more of a label and a collective rather than a group. He then doubled down on the &#8220;growth&#8221; aspect when asked how he felt about hearing that Rocky was a little upset about the situation. &#8220;I feel like that&#8217;s a personal thing for him,&#8221; he responded. &#8220;You could feel how you want to feel, but at the end of the day, it&#8217;s like I got to follow my truth for sure and how I feel. And there&#8217;s nothing wrong with growing.&#8221;

He then went on to explain that he made the choice in an effort to be his own man.

&#8220;I got A$AP tatted on me. I&#8217;ve always been Ferg. I&#8217;ve always been Ferg growing up,&#8221; he said. &#8220;When I came to work with the mob, that&#8217;s when I became A$AP Ferg. So now I&#8217;m just going back to who I am. Like now it&#8217;s like, &#8216;All right, we grown. You got kids, you doing your thing, and I&#8217;m over here doing my thing.&#8217; We&#8217;re not mobbing anymore. Like we&#8217;re grown. Let me show people what Ferg is about.&#8221;

He added: &#8220;Imagine if I&#8217;m moving around with them everywhere and going on Rocky tours and doing that thing, it&#8217;s like I&#8217;m not able to even bump into my blessings because I&#8217;m following somebody else&#8217;s dream. It&#8217;s like I got to go and do Ferg. People got to know who I am before I leave this earth.&#8221;

Back in January 2025 , Ferg confirmed his name change and said that A$AP was a thing of the past during a conversation with Touré.

“Well, I don’t think there is A$AP anymore,” Ferg said. “There’s not a&nbsp; Cozy Tape &nbsp;out; a new one. There’s not an office, there’s not a record label, A$AP Worldwide. I think it’s a thing of the past.”

